<% content_for :title, "Legal Terms and Conditions" %>
<% content_for :page_heading, "Legal Terms & Conditions" %>

<div class="hmHero">
  <span class="hmHero-eyebrow">Legal</span>
  <h1 class="hmHero-title">Legal Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
  <p class="hmHero-lead">Please review the rules and policies governing all <%= SITE_TITLE %> leagues below.</p>
</div>

<div data-controller="accordion">
  <div class="faqToolbar">
    <button type="button" class="hmBtn hmBtn--outline" data-action="accordion#expandAll">Expand All</button>
    <button type="button" class="hmBtn hmBtn--outline" data-action="accordion#collapseAll">Collapse All</button>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-8 ptfgPageWidth">
      <div class="faqAccordion">
        <%= render layout: "shared/accordion_item", locals: { id: 1, icon: "calendar-event", accent: "blue", links: true, question: "Tournament Schedules" } do %>
          For any reason, if the PGA modifies any portion of their season schedule, <%= PTFG_ABBR %> reserves the
          right to any league schedules impacted by the change. If a golf tournament is canceled, it will be removed
          from the schedule, and any golfer picks will be rolled back.  If all four rounds of a golf tournament are
          not completed, golfer winnings are assigned as per the tournament results. For leagues playing the
          <i>Pick 3 Classic</i> format (weekend subs), those winnings will be assigned based on the active lineups
          at the time the tournament was halted.
        <% end %>

        <%= render layout: "shared/accordion_item", locals: { id: 2, icon: "pencil-square", accent: "blue", question: "Lineup Submissions" } do %>
          Each week, participants must submit their lineup via the website prior to the posted deadline time for
          each tournament. Upon submitting a lineup, participants will receive a confirmation e-mail. Participants
          can also use the <b>Results</b> and <b>Lineup</b> pages to immediately confirm their lineup. With these
          mechanisms in place, it is the participant’s responsibility to ensure their lineup was successfully
          processed by the system.
        <% end %>

        <%= render layout: "shared/accordion_item", locals: { id: 3, icon: "clock", accent: "blue", question: "Lineup Deadlines" } do %>
          PTFG uses the Thursday tournament start time as the first round deadline. Participants should always
          check the website for updates regarding lineup deadlines. Scheduled lineup reminders are sent via e-mail
          each Wednesday morning with the lineup deadline included. For leagues playing the <i>Pick 3 Classic</i>
          format (weekend subs), 3rd and 4th round lineup deadline extensions due to weather delays will be posted
          on the website as needed. If a participant misses a deadline, league commissioners have the ability to
          update anyone's lineup at anytime (at their discretion).
        <% end %>

        <%= render layout: "shared/accordion_item", locals: { id: 4, icon: "trophy", accent: "blue", links: true, question: "Scoring" } do %>
          Weekly scores for each participant are computed based on their lineup submitted for the tournament. Each
          league's website is updated with the tournament results every Sunday evening. The
          <%= link_to "PGA Tour", "http://www.pgatour.com" %> tournament website is used for the official golfer
          earnings in USD. Any fractional dollar amounts (pennies) are truncated.
        <% end %>

        <%= render layout: "shared/accordion_item", locals: { id: 5, icon: "hammer", accent: "purple", links: true, question: "Rule Disputes" } do %>
          Any disputes or discrepancies regarding rules will be resolved by <%= SITE_TITLE %> based on its
          interpretation of the rules. <%= SITE_TITLE %> will consider the intent and spirit of the rules, the
          integrity of the content, as well as the feasibility of accommodating any appeal. All disputes must be
          submitted via email. The deadline for submitting a rule dispute is two days from the end date of the golf
          tournament for which the dispute occurred. All decisions made by <%= SITE_TITLE %> are final and binding.
          <%= SITE_TITLE %> reserves the right to modify any rules for clarification purposes without materially
          affecting the terms and conditions of the contest.
        <% end %>

        <%= render layout: "shared/accordion_item", locals: { id: 6, icon: "envelope", accent: "green", links: true, question: "Email Addresses" } do %>
          All league communication is performed via e-mail.  Therfore, all participants must have a valid email
          address. It is the sole responsibily of each articipant to notify their league commissioner if their
          e-mail address should change during the PTFG contest.  Only league commissioners can update other's email
          addresses.  As mentioned in the <i>Participant Privacy</i> section below, e-mail addresses are never
          displayed on the league website or shared with others.
        <% end %>

        <%= render layout: "shared/accordion_item", locals: { id: 7, icon: "key", accent: "green", links: true, question: "Password Privacy" } do %>
          Passwords used by contest participants are encrypted and cannot be retrieved by <%= SITE_TITLE %>
          employees. If a participant forgets or loses their password, they can request it be reset to a default
          value via e-mail.  After the reset, participants can change their password to whatever they want.
          Participants are responsible for the secrecy of their password. <%= SITE_TITLE %> is not responsible or
          liable for any actions taken by someone else using a participant's password and account.
        <% end %>

        <%= render layout: "shared/accordion_item", locals: { id: 8, icon: "shield-lock", accent: "green", links: true, question: "Participant Privacy" } do %>
          <%= SITE_TITLE %> does not share the  e-mail addresses of its participants with anyone.  We fully respect
          each participant’s privacy.  Only the league commissioner(s) can see another league member's email
          addresses. E-mail addresses are never displayed on public facing pages.
        <% end %>

        <%= render layout: "shared/accordion_item", locals: { id: 9, icon: "wifi-off", accent: "red", links: true, question: "Internet / Technology Issues" } do %>
          If for any reason, the <%= SITE_TITLE %> system is not capable of functioning as planned, including
          infection by computer virus, bugs, tampering, unauthorized intervention, fraud, technical failures or
          any other causes beyond the control of  <%= PTFG_ABBR %> which corrupt or affect the administration,
          security, fairness, integrity or proper conduct of the contest, <%= PTFG_ABBR %> reserves the right to
          modify the rules or suspend the <%= PTFG_ABBR %> contest.  <%= PTFG_ABBR %> assumes no responsibility
          for any error, omissions, interruption, deletion, defect or delay in operation with transmission,
          communications, line failure, theft, destruction or unauthorized access to the website.
        <% end %>

        <%= render layout: "shared/accordion_item", locals: { id: 10, icon: "people", accent: "red", links: true, question: "Personal Behavior" } do %>
          Participants agree to behave in a lawful, respectful, and sportsmanlike manner while using of the
          <%= SITE_TITLE %> website including, but not limited to, the clubhouse message board. Any conduct by a
          participant which is deemed by <%= PTFG_ABBR %> to threaten, harass, intimidate, offend or harm any
          participant or <%= PTFG_ABBR %> representative is strictly prohibited. <%= PTFG_ABBR %> reserves the
          right, in its sole discretion, to ban any person from further participation if they engage in such
          prohibited conduct.
        <% end %>

        <%= render layout: "shared/accordion_item", locals: { id: 11, icon: "bug", accent: "red", links: true, question: "Website Tampering" } do %>
          Any attempt by a participant or individual to deliberately damage the <%= SITE_TITLE %> website is a
          violation of criminal and civil law.  If such an event occurs, <%= PTFG_ABBR %> reserves the right to
          seek damages to the fullest extent of the law.
        <% end %>

        <%= render layout: "shared/accordion_item", locals: { id: 12, icon: "info-circle", accent: "purple", links: true, question: "Disclaimer" } do %>
          <%= SITE_TITLE %> is not responsible for any problem or technical malfunction which impedes or interferes
          with a transaction including but not limited to starting / sub lineup submissions.  <%= PTFG_ABBR %>
          is not responsible for the failure of any cable or DSL connectivity, computer servers, equipment,
          software, or traffic congestion on the Internet or any damage to a participant's computer related to or
          resulting from participation in <%= PTFG_ABBR %>.  <%= PTFG_ABBR %> is not responsible for any loss
          or liability incurred by any participant or for any unlawful behavior by a participant. <%= PTFG_ABBR %>
          is not associated with the Professional Golfers Association or any of its members, the PGA Tour, or any
          golf tournaments making up this contest.  <%= PTFG_ABBR %> is void where prohibited by law.
          All federal, state, local, and provincial laws and regulations apply. In the event that this contest is
          challenged by any legal or regulatory authority, <%= PTFG_ABBR %> reserves the right to discontinue or
          modify the contest, or to disqualify participants residing in the affected geographic areas. In such
          event, <%= PTFG_ABBR %> shall have no liability to any participants who are disqualified due to such an
          action.
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
    <%= render "layouts/right_logo" %>
  </div>
</div>
